  "description": "Dracaena fragrans 'Compacta' (often sold as Janet Craig Compacta) is a compact cultivar of Dracaena fragrans, native to tropical Africa. It belongs to the Asparagaceae family and forms dense rosettes of short, broad, glossy dark green leaves (typically 15-30 cm long), unlike the taller, arching foliage of the standard Corn Plant. Growth is upright and bushy, with a slow growth rate that makes it well-suited to terrariums and indoor displays. It tolerates low to medium light and moderate humidity. Like other Dracaena species, it is toxic if ingested. In terrariums it provides lush, tropical foliage without outgrowing the space quickly.",
